  "foaf:name": "Antarctic Penguin Populations",
  "sdo:name": "Antarctic Penguin Populations",
  "sdo:description": "MAPPPD is a data portal consisting of all open access, publicly available penguin census records around the Antarctic continent. Since its inception, MAPPPD has been used in over 100 peer-reviewed studies looking at penguin dynamics in Antarctica and has become a vital tool for conservation managers. Its role is to highlight gaps in where data are not publicly available, and also act as a portal for the public to access and digest population data in line with the goal of transparency advocated under the Antarctic Treaty.",
